<title>USA: Wisconsin unemployment holds at 3.5 pct for March.</title>
<headline>Wisconsin unemployment holds at 3.5 pct for March.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wisconsin's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate remained at 3.5 percent in March, the same as the previous month, the state Department of Workforce Development reported Monday.</p>
<p>Private employers added 13,800 jobs in March, almost twice the normal growth rate for the month, the department said.</p>
<p>Most of the increase came in trade, construction, service, transportation and public utilities areas.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, 312-408-8647))</p>
